---
description: Move or hide stock GNOME Shell widgets and restore them in disable(). Use when changing top bar or dash layout.
alwaysApply: false
---

# Stock widgets

Record visibility, parent, and index before hiding or moving a stock widget. Restore all three in `disable()`. `this._destination` is the box this feature chose. Remove a child from its current parent before inserting it elsewhere.

```javascript
enable() {
    const clock = Main.panel.statusArea.dateMenu;

    this._clock = clock;
    this._clockParent = clock.get_parent();
    this._clockIndex = this._clockParent.get_children().indexOf(clock);
    this._clockVisible = clock.visible;

    this._clockParent.remove_child(clock);
    this._destination.insert_child_at_index(clock, 0);
}

disable() {
    const clock = this._clock;
    const parent = this._clockParent;
    this._clock = null;
    this._clockParent = null;

    if (!clock)
        return;

    clock.get_parent()?.remove_child(clock);
    parent.insert_child_at_index(clock, this._clockIndex);
    clock.visible = this._clockVisible;
}
```

Destroy only actors this feature created. Null the field after `destroy()`. Destroying an actor twice throws.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
this._button.destroy();

// ✅ GOOD
this._button?.destroy();
this._button = null;
```

Use `Main.panel.addToStatusArea(this._extension.uuid, indicator)` only when the feature's job is a status indicator. Pass a unique name if that id is already taken.
